shade-backface.patch (2026-10-31, branch fix/shade-backface): toolkit changes on top of the toolkit patch of main ddbb4c1.

PS3RECOMP_ENG_SHADE_BACKFACE (live, default 1; 0 = v0.2.14; toggle after PS3T_ENG_SHADOW_D24): in
inFAMOUS 2's deferred composite (FP f384f111ad5956ba) a receiver without stencil bit 7 whose N.L is
negative reads the sun mask as 0 (shadowed). The world's sun-shadow casters are drawn second-depth
(cull FRONT, no polygon offset), so world surfaces turned away from the sun compared against their own
depth: the 2x2 PCF ramp printed as blue/dark dot grids and stair-steps through the unclamped
mask x sun x N.L. The program variant is part of the pipeline key, so a live change rebuilds it.
PS3RECOMP_ENG_BACKFACE_CASTER_BIAS=<N> (diagnostic, read once): cull-FRONT depth-only casters get a
depth bias of -N x slope, -1000 x N units (pulled towards the light; < 0 pushes them away).
Apply with: git apply -p1 inside ps3recomp-fork/.

